1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:01,779
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:05,860
In this lesson, we will make
alerts reach the intended audience.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:11,149
Repeated messages create noise, while
incomplete contacts and device preferences

4
00:00:11,149 --> 00:00:13,510
can leave intended recipients unreachable.

5
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:16,989
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,989 --> 00:00:18,879
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:23,020
An administrator creates notification
rules for new calls, builds an

8
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:27,649
Officers distribution list and runs a
communication test before going live.

9
00:00:28,149 --> 00:00:30,670
A dispatch only helps
if it reaches people.

10
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:34,229
This is where you confirm members
can actually be contacted.

11
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:38,230
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:40,449
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:40,669 --> 00:00:41,970
Notification rules.

14
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:47,089
Rules that alert chosen people when
calls, statuses or other events happen.

15
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:50,499
Create notification rules
for the events officers and

16
00:00:50,499 --> 00:00:52,140
administrators need to know about.

17
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:53,579
Distribution lists.

18
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:57,120
Reusable recipient lists,
including email lists.

19
00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:01,149
Create lists for groups you
message often, such as Officers.

20
00:01:01,309 --> 00:01:02,640
Communication Tests.

21
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:05,930
Test messages that show
whether members can be reached.

22
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:10,679
Run a communication test before
going live and after major changes.

23
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,249
Chat.

24
00:01:11,689 --> 00:01:13,040
Team chat for members.

25
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:16,410
Create channels for your
teams once chat is enabled.

26
00:01:16,669 --> 00:01:17,329
Inbox.

27
00:01:17,659 --> 00:01:18,830
Messages sent to you.

28
00:01:19,290 --> 00:01:22,600
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

29
00:01:22,659 --> 00:01:24,250
and installed the Responder app.

30
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:26,990
Availability also depends on Messaging.

31
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:29,499
Check access in the target department.

32
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:30,710
Sent Messages.

33
00:01:31,109 --> 00:01:32,359
Messages you have sent.

34
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:36,100
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

35
00:01:36,170 --> 00:01:37,850
and installed the Responder app.

36
00:01:38,249 --> 00:01:40,629
Availability also depends on Messaging.

37
00:01:41,049 --> 00:01:43,139
Check access in the target department.

38
00:01:43,330 --> 00:01:44,229
New Message.

39
00:01:44,579 --> 00:01:48,019
Send a message, poll or
callback request to members.

40
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:51,580
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

41
00:01:51,639 --> 00:01:53,210
and installed the Responder app.

42
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,960
Availability also depends on Messaging.

43
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:58,380
Check access in the target department.

44
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:00,960
Chatbot and Assistant
integration settings.

45
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:05,340
Connect the Rez grid Assistant to chat
platforms and choose what it may do.

46
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:09,040
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

47
00:02:09,099 --> 00:02:10,679
and installed the Responder app.

48
00:02:10,829 --> 00:02:15,410
Account linking associates a member with
a configured external assistant platform.

49
00:02:15,890 --> 00:02:20,190
Confirm a platform is configured,
generate a short-lived linking code, and

50
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:22,430
complete linking in the intended platform.

51
00:02:22,879 --> 00:02:25,989
Review the linked identity and
a controlled permitted action.

52
00:02:26,470 --> 00:02:28,879
Keep the temporary code
out of the recording.

53
00:02:29,369 --> 00:02:32,150
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

54
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:33,640
recording the live workflow.

55
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:36,659
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

56
00:02:37,129 --> 00:02:37,780
Step 1.

57
00:02:38,289 --> 00:02:41,459
Confirm member contacts and
notification preferences.

58
00:02:41,919 --> 00:02:42,560
Step 2.

59
00:02:43,119 --> 00:02:47,050
Create an Officers distribution list
and a focused notification rule.

60
00:02:47,539 --> 00:02:48,279
Step 3.

61
00:02:48,699 --> 00:02:52,710
Run an explicit communication test
and review the recorded outcomes.

62
00:02:52,919 --> 00:02:54,389
Now verify the result.

63
00:02:54,830 --> 00:02:58,789
Ask test recipients to confirm the
actual channel and time received.

64
00:02:59,209 --> 00:03:02,609
Review missing or failed results
and the intended audience.

65
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:07,810
A common problem to watch for: A provider
handoff is not confirmed delivery.

66
00:03:08,279 --> 00:03:12,470
Staffing suppression, recipient
selection, and contact eligibility

67
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:14,259
each deserve a separate check.

68
00:03:14,459 --> 00:03:16,059
Your practice task is simple.

69
00:03:16,409 --> 00:03:18,479
Send only to the demo audience.

70
00:03:18,809 --> 00:03:23,370
Record recipients, observed receipts,
failures, and follow-up actions;

71
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,540
compare with the expected audience.

72
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:29,769
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

73
00:03:30,139 --> 00:03:33,529
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
